module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveChart.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpace.IdealSheafOfHypersurface

/-!
# Dehomogenization on a standard chart of projective space

Let `R` be a commutative ring and let `j` be one of the homogeneous coordinates of
`P^n_R = Proj R[T₀, …, Tₙ]`.  `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.chartRingEquiv` identifies the `j`-th chart
ring with `R[Y₁, …, Yₙ]`; this file records what that identification does to the fraction
`F / T_j ^ d` attached to a homogeneous `F` of degree `d`.  It is the dehomogenization
`F(T_j = 1)`, and dehomogenization does not raise the total degree.

The consequence is the one a plane-curve argument needs. If `i : Z ⟶ P^n_R` is a closed immersion
whose homogeneous ideal is generated by a homogeneous `F` of degree `d`, then the kernel of `i`
over the standard open `D₊(T_j)` is generated by the dehomogenization of `F`, read in
`R[Y₁, …, Yₙ]` through the chart identification — a polynomial of total degree at most `d`. That
is the affine equation of `Z` on the chart, with its degree bound.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.dehomCoeff`: dehomogenization at the `j`-th variable, with coefficients
  read in `R` rather than in the degree-zero part of the grading.

## Main results

* `MvPolynomial.totalDegree_aeval_le`: substituting polynomials of total degree at most one for
  the variables does not raise the total degree.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.totalDegree_dehomCoeff_le`: dehomogenization does not raise the total
  degree.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.chartRingEquiv_dehomCoeff` and
  `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.sectionsChartEquiv_dehomCoeff`: the chart identification carries the
  dehomogenization of `F` to the fraction `F / T_j ^ d`, as an element of the chart ring and as a
  section of the structure sheaf.
* `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.ker_app_basicOpen_X_eq_span_dehomCoeff`: **the affine equation of a
  hypersurface on a chart** — for `I(Z) = (F)` the kernel of `i` over `D₊(T_j)` is generated by
  the image of the dehomogenization of `F`.

## Implementation notes

`Stacks.ProjectiveChart.dehom` is the inverse of `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.chartHom` and is already
available, but only as a one-sided inverse (`dehom_comp_chartHom`); since `chartHom` is bijective
that one-sided statement determines the inverse, which is
`Stacks.ProjectiveChart.chartRingEquivDeg0_symm_apply`.  Its value on
`HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk` is computed from the definition of `dehom` as an
`IsLocalization.Away.lift`, using that dehomogenization sends `T_j` to `1`.

The coefficients of `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.dehom` live in the degree-zero part of the grading;
`dehomCoeff` composes with `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.degreeZeroEquiv` to bring them back to `R`, and
is then simply the substitution `T_j ↦ 1`, `T_{j.succAbove a} ↦ Y_a`
(`Stacks.ProjectiveChart.dehomCoeff_eq_aeval`), which is the form the degree bound is proved in.

The total-degree bound is stated for an arbitrary substitution by polynomials of degree at most
one because Mathlib has no bound for `MvPolynomial.bind₁`; the proof is the sum-over-monomials
one, through `MvPolynomial.eval₂_eq`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0801](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0801)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry MvPolynomial

namespace Stacks.ProjectiveChart


universe u

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R]

attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra

/-- The inverse of `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.chartRingEquivDeg0` is
`Stacks.ProjectiveChart.dehom`. -/
theorem chartRingEquivDeg0_symm_apply {n : ℕ} (i : Fin (n + 1)) (u : ChartRing R n i) :
    (chartRingEquivDeg0 R i).symm u = dehom R i u := by
  calc (chartRingEquivDeg0 R i).symm u
      = (dehom R i).comp (chartHom R i).toRingHom ((chartRingEquivDeg0 R i).symm u) := by
        rw [dehom_comp_chartHom]
        rfl
    _ = dehom R i u := by
        rw [RingHom.comp_apply]
        exact congrArg (dehom R i) ((chartRingEquivDeg0 R i).apply_symm_apply u)

/-- Dehomogenization sends the fraction `F / T_i ^ d`, for `F` homogeneous of degree `d`, to the
dehomogenization `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.dehomPolynomial` of `F`. -/
theorem dehom_awayMk {n : ℕ} (i : Fin (n + 1)) (d : ℕ) (F : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) R)
    (hF : F ∈ MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R (d • 1)) :
    dehom R i (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk
        (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R) (X_mem_degree_one R i) d F hF)
      = dehomPolynomial R i F := by
  simp [dehom, dehomPolynomial, HomogeneousLocalization.algebraMap_apply,
    HomogeneousLocalization.Away.val_mk, IsLocalization.Away.lift, IsLocalization.lift_mk',
    IsUnit.liftRight_apply, Localization.mk_eq_mk']


/-- Substituting polynomials of degree at most one for the variables does not raise the total
degree. -/
theorem _root_.MvPolynomial.totalDegree_aeval_le {σ τ : Type*} {A : Type*} [CommSemiring A]
    (g : σ → MvPolynomial τ A) (hg : ∀ i, (g i).totalDegree ≤ 1) (F : MvPolynomial σ A) :
    (MvPolynomial.aeval g F).totalDegree ≤ F.totalDegree := by
  classical
  rw [MvPolynomial.aeval_def, MvPolynomial.eval₂_eq]
  refine MvPolynomial.totalDegree_finsetSum_le fun d hd => ?_
  refine (MvPolynomial.totalDegree_mul _ _).trans ?_
  rw [MvPolynomial.algebraMap_eq, MvPolynomial.totalDegree_C, zero_add]
  refine (MvPolynomial.totalDegree_finset_prod _ _).trans ?_
  refine (Finset.sum_le_sum fun i _ => (MvPolynomial.totalDegree_pow _ _).trans
    (Nat.mul_le_mul_left _ (hg i))).trans ?_
  simpa [Finsupp.sum] using MvPolynomial.le_totalDegree hd


/-- Dehomogenization at the `i`-th variable, with coefficients read in `R`. -/
def dehomCoeff {n : ℕ} (i : Fin (n + 1)) :
    MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) R →+* MvPolynomial (Fin n) R :=
  (MvPolynomial.mapEquiv (Fin n) (degreeZeroEquiv R n)).toRingHom.comp (dehomPolynomial R i)

/-- `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.dehomCoeff` is the substitution `T_i ↦ 1`,
`T_{i.succAbove a} ↦ Y_a`. -/
theorem dehomCoeff_eq_aeval {n : ℕ} (i : Fin (n + 1)) (F : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) R) :
    dehomCoeff R i F
      = MvPolynomial.aeval (fun k => (finSuccEquiv' i k).elim 1 MvPolynomial.X) F := by
  have : dehomCoeff R i
      = (MvPolynomial.aeval
          (fun k => (finSuccEquiv' i k).elim 1 MvPolynomial.X) :
            MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) R →ₐ[R] MvPolynomial (Fin n) R).toRingHom := by
    refine MvPolynomial.ringHom_ext (fun r => ?_) (fun k => ?_)
    · simp [dehomCoeff, dehomPolynomial]
    · cases h : finSuccEquiv' i k <;> simp [dehomCoeff, dehomPolynomial, h]
  exact congrArg (fun g => g F) this

/-- Dehomogenization does not raise the total degree. -/
theorem totalDegree_dehomCoeff_le [Nontrivial R] {n : ℕ} (i : Fin (n + 1))
    (F : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) R) : (dehomCoeff R i F).totalDegree ≤ F.totalDegree := by
  rw [dehomCoeff_eq_aeval]
  refine MvPolynomial.totalDegree_aeval_le _ (fun k => ?_) F
  cases h : finSuccEquiv' i k with
  | none => simp
  | some j => exact (MvPolynomial.totalDegree_X j).le

/-- The chart identification `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.chartRingEquiv` carries the
dehomogenization of a homogeneous `F` of degree `d` to the fraction `F / T_i ^ d`. -/
theorem chartRingEquiv_dehomCoeff {n : ℕ} (i : Fin (n + 1)) (d : ℕ)
    (F : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) R)
    (hF : F ∈ MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R (d • 1)) :
    chartRingEquiv R i (dehomCoeff R i F)
      = HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk
          (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R) (X_mem_degree_one R i) d F hF := by
  have h := chartRingEquivDeg0_symm_apply R i (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk
    (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R) (X_mem_degree_one R i) d F hF)
  rw [dehom_awayMk R i d F hF] at h
  have hmm : ∀ x : MvPolynomial (Fin n) (Deg0 R n),
      (MvPolynomial.mapEquiv (Fin n) (degreeZeroEquiv R n).symm)
        ((MvPolynomial.mapEquiv (Fin n) (degreeZeroEquiv R n)) x) = x := by
    intro x
    rw [← MvPolynomial.mapEquiv_symm]
    exact (MvPolynomial.mapEquiv (Fin n) (degreeZeroEquiv R n)).symm_apply_apply x
  rw [show chartRingEquiv R i (dehomCoeff R i F)
      = chartRingEquivDeg0 R i (dehomPolynomial R i F) by
    show chartRingEquivDeg0 R i (MvPolynomial.mapEquiv (Fin n) (degreeZeroEquiv R n).symm
        (MvPolynomial.mapEquiv (Fin n) (degreeZeroEquiv R n) (dehomPolynomial R i F)))
      = chartRingEquivDeg0 R i (dehomPolynomial R i F)
    exact congrArg (chartRingEquivDeg0 R i) (hmm _)]
  rw [← h, RingEquiv.apply_symm_apply]


/-- The identification `Stacks.ProjectiveChart.sectionsChartEquiv` carries the dehomogenization of
a homogeneous `F` of degree `d` to the section `F / T_i ^ d` of the structure sheaf over `D₊(T_i)`.
-/
theorem sectionsChartEquiv_dehomCoeff {n : ℕ} (i : Fin (n + 1)) (d : ℕ)
    (F : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) R)
    (hF : F ∈ MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R (d • 1)) :
    sectionsChartEquiv R i (dehomCoeff R i F)
      = AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.chartFraction
          (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R) (X_mem_degree_one R i) d
          ⟨F, hF⟩ := by
  rw [sectionsChartEquiv, RingEquiv.trans_apply, chartRingEquiv_dehomCoeff R i d F hF]
  rfl


/-- **The affine equation of a hypersurface on a standard chart.**  If the homogeneous ideal of a
closed subscheme `Z ⊆ P^n_R` is generated by a homogeneous `F` of degree `d`, then the kernel of
`i : Z ⟶ P^n_R` over the standard open `D₊(T_j)` is generated by the image of the dehomogenization
of `F` under the chart identification.  Its total degree is at most `d`, by
`Stacks.ProjectiveChart.totalDegree_dehomCoeff_le`. -/
theorem ker_app_basicOpen_X_eq_span_dehomCoeff [IsNoetherianRing R] {n : ℕ} (j : Fin (n + 1))
    {Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (i : Z ⟶ AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R))
    [AlgebraicGeometry.IsClosedImmersion i] {d : ℕ} (F : MvPolynomial (Fin (n + 1)) R)
    (hF : F ∈ MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R (d • 1))
    (hideal : AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.idealOfClosedSubscheme
      (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R) i = Ideal.span {F}) :
    RingHom.ker (i.app (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.basicOpen
          (MvPolynomial.homogeneousSubmodule (Fin (n + 1)) R) (MvPolynomial.X j))).hom
      = Ideal.span {sectionsChartEquiv R j (dehomCoeff R j F)} := by
  rw [sectionsChartEquiv_dehomCoeff R j d F hF]
  exact
    AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.ker_app_basicOpen_of_idealOfClosedSubscheme_eq_span _
    (MvPolynomial.adjoin_homogeneousSubmodule_one_eq_top (Fin (n + 1)) R)
    (X_mem_degree_one R j) i ⟨F, hF⟩ hideal

end Stacks.ProjectiveChart

end
